---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const repo=process.env.REPOSITORY_URL||'https://github.com/MuneefMumthas/hatrack';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/,'');
---
<Layout title="Download Hatrack for Windows | Multiple Claude & Codex Desktop accounts" description="Download the free Hatrack installer for Windows 11 x64. Run multiple Claude Desktop and Codex Desktop accounts without developer tools or a terminal."><article class="article"><h1>Download Hatrack<br/>for Windows</h1><p class="lead">Hatrack is a free desktop profile manager for Windows 11 x64 that runs multiple Claude Desktop and Codex Desktop accounts. You don’t need .NET, Node, or a terminal to use it.</p><a class="button" href={repo+'/releases'}>View Windows releases</a><p class="fine">Choose <code>Hatrack-Setup.exe</code>, not the source-code ZIP.</p><aside><strong>Preview release status</strong><p>The source and installer are being prepared for publication. A public download exists only after the maintainer publishes release assets. Independent authenticated Claude and Codex desktop sessions must pass acceptance before a stable release.</p></aside><h2>What happens after download?</h2><ol><li>Run the installer and open Hatrack.</li><li>Let it detect your desktop apps, or choose their location manually.</li><li>Create a profile, pick an icon, and choose shortcuts.</li><li>Open it and sign in inside the official app.</li></ol><h2>If an app is missing</h2><p>Hatrack links to the vendor’s official download. Install the original desktop app, leave Hatrack open, and detection resumes automatically.</p><h2>Signing and compatibility</h2><p>Initial builds are unsigned unless the maintainer configures a signing certificate. The release notes state the signing status and tested versions. Windows SmartScreen may warn about an unsigned installer; choose More info, then Run anyway only if you downloaded it from this project’s GitHub Releases page. Do not disable Windows security protections. Only desktop editions are targeted.</p><p><a href={`${base}/guides/`}>Read setup and troubleshooting guides →</a></p></article></Layout>
